.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH scanr-run 1  "scanr-run " 
.SH NAME
scanr\-run \- Execute a scan
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBscanr\-run\fR [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-transport\fR] [\fB\-\-targets\fR] [\fB\-\-ports\fR] [\fB\-\-pairs\fR] [\fB\-\-resumed\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\fR] [\fB\-\-concurrency\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\fR] [\fB\-\-retries\fR] [\fB\-\-dns\fR] [\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-seed\fR] [\fB\-\-open\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-compress\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-compress\fR] [\fB\-\-spans\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-spans\fR] [\fB\-\-banner\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-banner\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tls\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-versions\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tls\-versions\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-large\-range\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fISCAN\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Execute a scan
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
Timing profile: proxy\-careful, proxy, direct, direct\-fast, or one you defined
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI<TRANSPORT>\fR
Transport name
.TP
\fB\-\-targets\fR \fI<SPEC|FILE|\->\fR
Targets: specs, a named set, a file path, or `\-` for stdin (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-ports\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Ports: `80`, `1\-1024`, `all`, or a named set (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-pairs\fR \fI<FILE|\->\fR
Exact `host:port` endpoints from `scanr output remainder`; a file, or `\-` for stdin. IPv6 must be bracketed. Cannot be combined with \-\-targets or \-\-ports
.TP
\fB\-\-resumed\-from\fR \fI<SCAN_ID>\fR
The scan_id this run continues, recorded in the record so a resumed scan can be traced back. Picked up automatically from `scanr output remainder`
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fI<SPEC|FILE>\fR
Targets to exclude after expansion (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-concurrency\fR \fI<N>\fR
In\-flight probes; also the worker thread count
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\fR \fI<N>\fR
Launch rate ceiling in probes/second, 0 for unlimited
.TP
\fB\-\-connect\-timeout\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR
Destination connection timeout, e.g. 2s or 500ms
.TP
\fB\-\-retries\fR \fI<N>\fR
Retries for probes that time out
.TP
\fB\-\-dns\fR \fI<MODE>\fR
Who resolves hostnames
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Directory for JSONL scan records
.TP
\fB\-\-seed\fR \fI<HEX>\fR
Permutation seed, so a randomized scan can be replayed exactly
.TP
\fB\-\-open\-only\fR
Print only open ports (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Print every probe result, not just open ports
.TP
\fB\-\-compress\fR
Write the record as gzip (default). Roughly 20x smaller; `zcat`, `zless` and `scanr output` read it unchanged
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-compress\fR
Write the record as plain JSONL, so it can be grepped directly
.TP
\fB\-\-spans\fR
Collapse repetitive closed/filtered results into span events instead of one row each (default). Much smaller records; drops per\-probe timestamps for those
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-spans\fR
Write one row per probe, keeping every timestamp
.TP
\fB\-\-banner\fR
Read what open services volunteer on connect, without sending anything (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-banner\fR
Do not read banners
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\fR
Send a ClientHello offering TLS 1.3 and 1.2 to open ports that volunteered no banner and record the certificate, cipher and ALPN that come back. The one active probe scanr has; off by default
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tls\fR
Do not send the TLS probe (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-versions\fR
After the hello, ask SSLv2, SSLv3, TLS 1.0, 1.1 and 1.2 for themselves on their own connections, and say when only something old is spoken. Needs \-\-tls; up to five more connections per silent open port
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tls\-versions\fR
Do not survey protocol versions (default)
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-large\-range\fR
Permit target sets larger than 4,000,000 addresses
.TP
\fB\-\-full\fR
Show banners untruncated as they arrive (still printable ASCII only); the default cuts them at 48 characters so each result stays on one line
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fISCAN\fR]
Name of a scan defined in configuration; omit for an ad\-hoc scan
